## Fix round 1 — Optimizer execution-ceiling propagation

### Status

Completed and committed.

Commit: `adcda5f27ce31e1a545a2e7694cfa67bb0cf3f8c`
(`Propagate PIT optimizer execution limits`)

No tests were added, modified, or run. No provider, Docker, hidden-data,
network, push, upload, or subagent action was used.

### Review finding and correction

The schema-v3 CLI admitted `child_timeout_seconds` and `output_limit_bytes`,
but the canary dispatch passed only API and wall values into the live builder.
The disposable policy worker consequently retained its legacy 900-second fold
timeout, and regenerated canary commands omitted all four timeout/output
settings.

The correction keeps the legacy worker defaults intact while making the full
optimizer-specific `PitOptimizerLoopLimits` object effective in the active v3
path:

- `_dispatch_pit_optimizer_v3` now receives and validates the exact optimizer
  limits before passing them to the live-service builder.
- `_build_pit_optimizer_v3_live_run` consumes that limits object directly.
  API timeout configures the gateway; child timeout configures the disposable
  worker fold; output bytes cap Docker control capture and the interactive
  policy-worker session; and one absolute wall deadline is shared by provider
  calls, worker control/session work, and evaluator boundary checks.
- `PolicyWorkerRunner` accepts optimizer child/output/wall bounds. Its defaults
  remain the prior 900-second fold, 64-KiB Docker-control capture, and no
  absolute wall deadline for unchanged legacy callers.
- `PolicyWorkerSession` counts worker stdout and stderr, fails closed after the
  configured ceiling, and bounds each response wait by both the remaining fold
  time and the absolute run wall deadline.
- Trusted evaluator construction and candidate/baseline fold execution check
  the same wall deadline immediately before and after work. Candidate policy
  execution additionally receives that absolute deadline in its disposable
  worker session.
- `_pit_optimizer_v3_prepare_lines` now serializes max calls, max tokens,
  iterations, API timeout, child timeout, wall timeout, and output bytes from
  the validated optimizer limits. It still emits no USD option.
- The audit-only active controller still contains no hidden-evaluation
  invocation.

### Files changed

- `agent_loop.py` only: 225 insertions, 28 deletions.
- No test file and no other production file changed in this fix round.

